server, ntdll: Accept each owner of the folders of Wine on request.

Lepton, the Android container of the Steam Frame, shows each file with
the owner 0, and the app gets another uid from getuid. The tests of the
owner of the prefix, of its parent and of the folder of the server then
stop wineserver and each program ("... is not owned by you"). With
WINE_BWVR_ANY_OWNER=1 in the environment these tests accept each owner.
The test of the mode (no access for other users) stays. The app sets the
variable only when the owner of its own folder is not its uid
(wine_owner_check=2), or always (wine_owner_check=0).
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -1314,6 +1314,16 @@
 }
 
 
+/* A container that shows each file with the owner 0 to a process with
+ * another uid (Lepton of the Steam Frame) fails the owner tests of the
+ * folders of Wine. WINE_BWVR_ANY_OWNER=1 lets those tests accept each
+ * owner. The app sets it only when its own folder has another owner. */
+static int bwvr_owner_ok( uid_t owner )
+{
+    const char *any = getenv( "WINE_BWVR_ANY_OWNER" );
+    return owner == getuid() || (any && !strcmp( any, "1" ));
+}
+
